  "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of pupils in school year 9 that state that they have used different tobacco-/nicotine products at the age of 13 or younger.Question: 'How old were you when you (if ever) did the following things the first time?: 'smoked a cigarette', 'used snuff', 'vaped'. The indicator refers to the percentage that chose '11 years or younger', '12 years' or '13 years' on following options:- 'smoked cigarette'- 'used snuff'- 'vaped'- 'smoked cigarette' and/or 'used snuff'- 'smoked cigarette' and/or 'used snuff' and/or 'vaped'"
  ]
